<div class="legal-document" id="recruiter-privacy-policy">
  <h1 class="legal-document-title">Recruiter Userscript Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-document-subtitle">Last updated: <%= Date.today.strftime("%d %B %Y") %></p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-introduction">Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Bram, the creator of TornManager. This Privacy Policy covers the <strong>TornManager Recruiter
      userscript</strong>. That is the script you install in a userscript manager (such as Tampermonkey) or in
      Torn PDA. It runs on Torn.com pages and helps you find recruitable players in Torn companies.
    </p>
    <p>
      The TornManager web platform at tornmanager.com has its own <a href="#privacy-policy">Platform Privacy
      Policy</a> and <a href="#terms-of-service">Platform Terms of Service</a>, and the TornManager Chats
      userscript has its own <a href="#userscript-privacy-policy">Chats Userscript Privacy Policy</a> and
      <a href="#userscript-terms-of-service">Chats Userscript Terms of Service</a>, above on this page. If you
      only use Recruiter, this document and the
      <a href="#recruiter-terms-of-service">Recruiter Terms of Service</a> are the ones that apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-information-i-collect">Information I Collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in to Recruiter you provide your <strong>Torn API key</strong>, and only Public access keys
      are accepted. Signing in requires an active TornManager subscription. The key is sent to my server once to
      check who you are with the official Torn API and to verify your subscription, and it
      <strong>joins Recruiter's shared fetching pool</strong> (see The Key Pool below) &mdash; signing in is your
      consent for that. After that first check, your browser holds a <strong>session token</strong> and uses it
      for every later request; your API key itself is not sent again by the browser.
    </p>
    <p>On the server, a Recruiter account consists of:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Torn ID, player name, and level</li>
      <li>Your Torn API key (as the sign-in credential)</li>
      <li>API keys you contributed to the shared key pool, together with who contributed them</li>
      <li>Xanax payments sent for subscriptions, and subscription expiration dates</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Recruiter shares this account with the TornManager Chats userscript: one account and one subscription cover
      both scripts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-key-pool">The Key Pool</h2>
    <p>
      Recruiter uses a shared pool of Torn API keys for its background fetching. Your own key joins the pool
      when you sign in, and keys you add on the Keys screen are <strong>sent to and stored on the TornManager
      server</strong>, together with who contributed them. Pool keys are used exclusively for calls to the
      official Torn API on Recruiter's behalf.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every Torn API call carries the comment <code>tmrecruiter</code>, so the owner of any key can see in their
      own Torn key log exactly what their key was used for. The pool accepts only Public access keys and at most
      one key per player, matching how Torn's rate limit works. Only add keys that their owners gave you
      willingly. You can revoke a key on the Keys screen at any time, which stops all use of it, and a key owner
      can revoke access themselves by deleting or regenerating their key on Torn.com.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-torn-api">Calls to the Torn API</h2>
    <p>
      The TornManager server fetches publicly available game data from api.torn.com using the key pool: company
      listings and ratings, which players work where, player factions, Hall of Fame working stats, and the online
      status of employees. This data is refreshed daily, stored on the server, and served to every Recruiter
      subscriber. Your browser no longer calls the Torn API itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-local-storage">Data Stored in Your Browser</h2>
    <p>Recruiter stores the following in your browser's localStorage on the torn.com domain:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>User profile and session token</strong> (<code>rc_user</code>): your Torn ID, name, and the session token used for authentication. Cleared when you sign out.</li>
      <li><strong>Settings</strong> (<code>rc_settings</code>): your company type and star filters.</li>
      <li><strong>Subscription state</strong> (<code>rc_subscription</code>): the last known subscription status.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Signing out clears your session. Clearing localStorage for torn.com removes everything listed above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-backend">Backend Communication</h2>
    <p>
      Recruiter talks to tornmanager.com using <code>GM.xmlHttpRequest</code>: signing in, checking your
      subscription, loading recruiting matches and employee statuses, and managing the key pool. Requests after
      sign-in carry your session token. Nothing is shared with any third party.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-data-security">Data Security &amp; Location</h2>
    <p>
      All communication with tornmanager.com uses secure HTTPS connections. Server data is stored in
      <strong>Helsinki, Finland</strong> (EU) within the Hetzner datacenter, which means your data falls under
      European Union data protection laws, including GDPR. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.
      I work hard to protect your data, but I cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    <p>
      To remove your account and API key from the TornManager server, contact me on Torn:
      <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank", class: "player-link" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-age-requirement">Age Requirement</h2>
    <p>
      In line with Torn's Terms of Service, you must be at least 13 years old to use Recruiter.
      I do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-changes">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes are shown by updating the
      "Last updated" date at the top. If you keep using Recruiter after changes, you accept the updated policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rpp-contact">Contact Me</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how I handle your data, please reach out to me on Torn:
    </p>
    <p>
      <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank", class: "player-link" %>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
